      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">RTO Documentation &amp; Statutory Requirements for Delhi‑Mumbai Vehicle Moves</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;">**Mandatory Documentation Checklist for Delhi‑to‑Mumbai Car Transport**

1. **Registration Certificate (RC) – Original**  
   • Verify the RC is current and free of liens.  
   • Missing RC can lead to a ₹5,000 fine and vehicle seizure at the destination.

2. **Insurance Copy – Valid for the Journey**  
   • Include the original policy cover sheet and claim number.  
   • Without proof of insurance, the transport company may refuse pickup and you could face ₹10,000 penalty.

3. **Pollution Under‑Control (PUC) Certificate – Current**  
   • Must be issued within the last 90 days.  
   • A stale PUC can result in a ₹3,000 fine and impoundment of the vehicle.

4. **Original Invoice / Purchase Receipt**  
   • Confirms ownership and vehicle value.  
   • Absence may trigger a ₹2,500 penalty and delay in customs clearance if the vehicle is new.

5. **RTO Transfer Forms (Form 29 & 30) – Completed**  
   • Transfer of ownership to the transport company (if required).  
   • Incomplete forms can incur a ₹4,000 fine and delay the transfer process.

6. **Vehicle Inspection Report (VIR) – Signed by Your Agent**  
   • Records pre‑move condition to avoid disputes on arrival.  
   • Unreported damages may lead to ₹5,000 deduction from the final invoice.

7. **Power of Attorney (if you’re not the owner)**  
   • Grants legal authority to the mover to act on your behalf.  
   • Missing POA may result in a ₹3,000 penalty and denial of pickup.

**Common Pitfalls & Penalties**

